<binaryimage arch="x86:LE:64:default:gcc">
<!--
    kuna issue testcase: the Listing walk reads a Thumb tbb/tbh switch table
    (`option thumbswitch on|off`, default-ON).

    Issue:      kuna GH-299 - aif plants mid-function entries; on Cortex-M
                firmware most of them sit in switch case bodies behind a
                tbb/tbh the walk could not follow.
    Stage:      P1 code/data partition - the Listing walk's computed-jump
                successors (`listing/kuna_thumbswitch.rs`).
    P0 assert:  `option thumbswitch on|off`.

    The XML wrapper only provides the harness architecture.  Every pass clears
    it and loads `thumbswitch_le32` (generator `thumbswitch_le32.py` beside it):
    a stripped Thumb ELF whose vector table makes `_start` the reset handler.
    `_start` calls 22 leaves that open with `push {r4,lr}; movs r4,#n`,
    `dispatch` at 0x8226 (`cmp r0,#3; bhi default; tbb [pc,r0]`, four cases),
    `dispatch2` at 0x8254 (`cmp r0,#3; bcs default2; tbb [pc,r0]`, three
    cases, then a zero pad byte) and `dispatch3` at 0x8274 (`cmp r0,#3; bge
    default3; tbb [pc,r0]`, three cases, then a byte that reads as an offset
    to the unreferenced `lone3` at 0x8290).  Case 1 of the first two, at
    0x8238 and 0x8264, opens with the leaves' prologue and ends in its own
    `pop {r4,pc}`.

    Pass 1 (`mode aggressive`, `option thumbswitch off`) reproduces the bug:
    the walk stops at every tbb, and the gap walk lists both case bodies as
    sub_8238 and sub_8264.
    Pass 2 (`mode aggressive`, shipped default) reads the first two tables,
    four entries behind the bhi and three behind the bcs, decodes the cases as
    the dispatchers' code, and lists neither.  The signed bge bounds nothing,
    so `dispatch3`'s table is not read and `lone3` stays a function.
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x100000" readonly="true">
c3
</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x100000" name="harness_stub"/>
</binaryimage>
<script>
  <com>clear architecture</com>
  <com>load file decompiler/crates/kuna-analysis/tests/fixtures/thumbswitch_le32</com>
  <com>mode aggressive</com>
  <com>option thumbswitch off</com>
  <com>read symbols</com>
  <com>functions</com>
  <com>clear architecture</com>
  <com>load file decompiler/crates/kuna-analysis/tests/fixtures/thumbswitch_le32</com>
  <com>mode aggressive</com>
  <com>read symbols</com>
  <com>functions</com>
  <com>phase catalog thumbswitch</com>
  <com>quit</com>
</script>
